{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117098","id":3358115504,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7IKMaw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117098","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117098.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117098.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117098","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117098/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117098/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117098/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2dd1f4ef604608c46fa42c2dd2df1055fee5c48b","number":117098,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Decouple `node.h` from `scene_tree.h`, minimize its other includes","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Helps address #111218.\r\n- *Edit:* Merged. ~Includes #117097~.\r\n\r\nMy starting point was to try to minimize the includes in `node.h` to reduce its weight as a gateway for transitive includes throughout all of scene/editor.\r\n\r\nDoing so I could remove `scene_tree.h` by extracting the `SceneTree::Group` struct to a top-level `SceneTreeGroup`, which allows forward-declaring it and `SceneTree`. The leads to having to include `scene_tree.h` explicitly in a ton of .cpp files. Some are done in #117097 (because they already explicitly used it), and the rest are done in this PR due to the fact that `Node::get_tree()` no longer comes with batteries included (and it's often used as `get_tree()->do_stuff()` which hides the dependency on `SceneTree` from human/script eyes.\r\n\r\nFor an incremental rebuild after modifying `scene_tree.h`:\r\n\r\n- Before: 00:02:38.40\r\n- After: 00:00:51.79\r\n\r\nOther changes in this PR include:\r\n\r\n- Hardcode some `NOTIFICATION_*` values which used to be fetched from `SceneTree` or `MainLoop`, with a comment to keep them in sync (notably in `CanvasItem` and `Node3D`).\r\n- Adding back a few forward-declares which used to be inherited from `scene_tree.h`, such as `ArrayMesh`, `Material` or `PackedScene`.\r\n- Removing `message_queue.h` from `node.h`, which requires adding it in a few places where it's used explicitly.\r\n- Remove `SceneStringName(path_pp)` which was only used in a couple non-hot paths, so `scene_string_names.h` doesn't need to include `NodePath`, so it can be forward-declared in `node.h`.\r\n- Minor forward-declare tweaks to `core` dependencies of `node.h`. There's still more to do.\r\n- To remove the dependency on `SceneTree` in `node.h`, I had to move `Node::is_physics_interpolated_and_enabled` to the .cpp, which means it's no longer `_FORCE_INLINE_`. I'm not equipped to profile whether this makes a performance difference but it's worth considering. Additionally, it would be nice if we could forward-declare `SceneTreeFTI` in `scene_tree.h` and move the include to the .cpp, but currently it's added as a full member so we can't. Could it be made a pointer? CC @lawnjelly \r\n- One thing I couldn't manage to do is remove `input_event.h` from `node.h`, as it's used in `RequiredParam<T>` which currently needs a fully defined type (despite having some logic that aims to support forward-declares, but the use of `std::is_base_of_v` doesn't seem compatible with it).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner